  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy Transmission and Regional Integration Programme Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Action &#xBF;Energy Transmission and Regional Integration Programme Georgia&#xBF; will continue the open programme approach of the already completed Black Sea Transmission Project co-financed by EU NIF (No ENPI/2008/172059) and the &quot;Open Programme Extension of the Transmission Network, Phase II&quot; (OP II), which is under implementation and financed in the context of German Financial Cooperation with Georgia through KfW, co-financed by EU NIF (No ENI/2017/390-659 &#xBF;Extension of the Georgian Transmission Network&#xBF;) and EBRD. The overall objectives of the proposed Programme are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;1. Provision of modern energy-efficient resilient grid infrastructure according to European standards for the promotion of net integration of RES (Renewable Energy Sources) generation;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;2. Increase of transmission capacities, including domestic and cross-border trade which will also facilitate the implementation of regional priority projects (e.g. support to the Black Sea cable project) and synchronisation of the Georgian system with the European Network of Transmission System Operators for Electricity (ENTSO-E)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;3. Further improvement of security of energy supply in the light of a high proportion of RES generation injection to the grid in the foreseeable future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
